WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.730
 When I came out to my artist friends as wanting to be a cook, nobody was surprised.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:24.050
 They were like, "Well, you've been feeding us all this time," because it was kind of a moment of shame for me, you know, because I was just like, "I'm giving up."

00:00:24.050 --> 00:00:40.460
 I think I lost interest in dining out, you know, dining with a capital D, and I just started to feel like there's something really noble about home cooking, and that there's really a need for it, there's really a need for information about how to make food at home.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:01:11.350
 I mean, it's an interesting antidote to our modern kind of world, to think about having something like a boiled turnip ask you to take pause and consider its flavor and texture, you know, but then when that turnip becomes, you know, a way to understand a splash of like really vibrant, grassy, delicious olive oil, why is that moment

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:16.640
 less valid than, you know, a more complicated one?

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:19.200
 And is that more complicated even?

